  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fair Recovery &#x2013; Strengthened Civil Society and Media for Fiscal Justice in Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will build on work with the Media Foundation for West Africa (MFWA) and Africa Centre for Energy Policy (ACEP) to strengthen the fiscal justice capacity of investigative journalists. A media fellowship component will be attached to the partner organizations at national (ACEP, MFWA)) and subnational levels (Friends of the Nation, Norsaac) and a flexible fund will be set up to provide grants for investigative journalists to pursue promising stories. The project will focus on three outcomes: The first to build the capacity of civil society and investigative journalists; the second to achieve progressive and gender sensitive Disaster Risk Management (DRM); and third to increase pro -poor and gender sensitive budgets and address the debt crisis.</narrative>
  </description>
